  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cook rice blend: Fill a medium saucepan three-quarters full with water and bring to the boil. Add the rice blend and cook for 22-24 mins until tender. Drain and rinse under cold water.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4220454/photos/large/cook_grain_blend-3f4fc5b69d54d14c1ad93ee4f291d8f3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, coarsely grate the carrot. Crush half the garlic. Put the garlic, yoghurt, half the sumac and 1 tbs water in a bowl. Season with salt and pepper and stir to combine. Put the remaining sumac, 1 tbs olive oil, 2 tsp balsamic vinegar and 2 tsp honey in a large bowl and stir to combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4220455/photos/large/prep_ingredients-8574f5cb0143ba8809271b311e632830.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast pistachios: Put the pistachios in a cold medium frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 3-4 mins until evenly golden (see Kitchen 101). Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4220456/photos/large/toast_pistachios-1c8937714c0f2e46b23c66ed8604550c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook falafel: Heat 1 tbs olive oil in the same pan over medium-high heat. Cook the falafel, turning regularly, for 3-5 mins until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4220457/photos/large/cook_falafels-fd70b89e8375a12b94f68dd94f6d201c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Coarsely chop the pistachios. Add the rice blend, carrot and rocket to the vinaigrette and toss to combine. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the salad among bowls. Top with the pistachios and falafel and drizzle with the sumac yoghurt. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4220458/photos/large/serve_up-46c7f6d7ae6bcf42ce543eb3dc022706.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Starting with a cold pan ensures the nuts toast evenly and prevents them burning.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4220459/photos/large/kitchen_101-ac7f36780c24cb36dd3e9fcebe4e8fb3.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
